    {
      "beat_id": "B01",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. Ions in one trap do not need a wire between every pair. Their Coulomb-coupled motion forms collective vibrational modes, and laser forces can use those shared modes to mediate spin-spin gates.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Explain how distant trapped-ion qubits share a motional bus.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — ION TRAPS",
            "segment": "Collective Modes as a Bus",
            "greeting": "Szia, Liam",
            "runningText": "following spin-dependent forces through the chain…",
            "output": [
              "Ion motion decomposes into collective normal modes.",
              "Laser forces use those modes to create effective spin coupling."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B01.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B01.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.08,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B01.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B02",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "A chain of confined ions has many normal modes. In one mode the ions move together; in others neighboring ions move with different phases and amplitudes.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "accumulate"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B02.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.47,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B02.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B03",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "No one mode belongs to a single ion. Each normal mode is a collective coordinate with a participation pattern across the chain.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B03.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 8.19,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B03.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B04",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "State-dependent laser forces couple selected ion spins to that shared motion. A carefully shaped pulse makes the joint spin state acquire a conditional phase through the motional dynamics.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "branch"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B04.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.39,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B04.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B05",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "In a well-designed gate, the motional trajectory closes by the end. The modes disentangle from the spins, while the desired spin-spin entanglement remains.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "collapse"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B05.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 9.3,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B05.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B06",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Because multiple ions participate in shared modes, non-neighbor pairs can often be coupled without inserting a literal chain of nearest-neighbor SWAP gates. That is flexible connectivity, not free perfect all-to-all wiring.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "compare"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B06.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 13.21,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B06.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B07",
      "estimated_duration_s": 12,
      "narration_text": "Gate strength and fidelity depend on mode spectrum, ion participation, chain size, pulse shaping, heating, and crosstalk. Different pairs need not have identical speed or error.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "threshold"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B07.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.88,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B07.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B08",
      "estimated_duration_s": 11,
      "narration_text": "The bus is also not always only the center-of-mass mode. Practical entangling gates can involve one or several collective modes, with residual motion carefully canceled.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "GRAPHIC",
        "source": "own",
        "motion": "transform"
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B08.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 10.22,
      "build": {
        "status": "MANIM",
        "src": "manim/B08.mp4",
        "filled_by": "manim",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B09",
      "estimated_duration_s": 13,
      "narration_text": "Your turn. What must be true at the end of a clean shared-mode gate? Pause before the answer: the spin state keeps the conditional phase, while the motional modes return to a spin-independent final state and disentangle.",
      "shot": {
        "type": "CARD",
        "source": "remotion",
        "motion": "type",
        "remotion": {
          "pattern": "ClaudeComposerAsk",
          "props": {
            "command": "Your turn: close the motional loop.",
            "topic": "QUANTUM MECHANICS — CHECK",
            "segment": "Keep the Phase, Release the Bus",
            "greeting": "Over to you, Liam",
            "runningText": "waiting for the end-of-gate condition…",
            "output": [
              "Spin system retains the entangling phase.",
              "Motion closes its trajectory and disentangles from spin."
            ],
            "folderLabel": "@NikBearBrown",
            "modelLabel": "Claude",
            "effortLabel": "High"
          },
          "rendered": {
            "out": "media/B09.mp4",
            "at": ""
          }
        }
      },
      "audio_file": "mp3/beat-B09.mp3",
      "actual_duration_s": 11.86,
      "build": {
        "status": "VIDEO",
        "src": "media/B09.mp4",
        "filled_by": "media",
        "at": "2026-07-19T00:01:19"
      }
    },
    {
      "beat_id": "B10",
      "estimated_duration_s": 8,
      "narration_text": "Every ion shares one spring — more precisely, a family of collective modes that can serve as a temporary quantum bus.",
